course: dictionary
lesson: 4621
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Highly» has three main jobs, and the words around it tell you which one you need. Read the sentence first, then choose the meaning that fits.
explain: Meaning one is very or very much. «It is highly unlikely to rain today» means it is very unlikely to rain. «Highly dangerous» means very dangerous. Here highly makes the next word stronger.
explain: Meaning two is with great respect or praise. «In the UK people value queuing highly and get upset about queue-jumping» means people think queuing is very important. «I think highly of my teacher» means I admire and respect her.
explain: Meaning three is at a high level, rank or amount. «Highly skilled» means very good at something, and «highly paid» means earning a lot of money. The words after highly are the clues: a skill, a job or a level tells you this meaning is the right one.
fact: Highly can mean very or very much: «highly unlikely» means almost impossible.
fact: Highly can mean with great respect: «think highly of someone» means to admire them.
fact: Highly can mean at a high level, rank or amount: «highly skilled» means very good at something.
fact: Labels such as «highly flammable» warn you that something catches fire very easily, so keep it away from flames.
fact: A good check is to swap in «very» and see if the sentence still makes sense. If it does, the first meaning fits.
exercise: «In the UK people value queuing highly and get upset about queue-jumping.» What does highly mean here? | Higher than a building | Very quickly | *Very much, or with great respect | Not at all
exercise: A label on a bottle says «highly flammable». What should you do? | Put it in your school bag | *Keep it away from fire | Eat it with your lunch | Light it for a fun party
exercise: «She is highly skilled at chess.» What does highly mean? | Very loud | Upside down | *At a high level: she is very good | Very sad
test: «It is highly unlikely to rain today.» What does this tell you? | It will be sunny and warm | *Rain is very unlikely to happen | Rain is very likely | It is raining right now
test: Ella says, «I think highly of my neighbour.» What does she feel? | Bored of her | *She respects and admires her | Afraid of her | Cross with her
exam: «The machine is highly dangerous, so only trained staff may use it.» What does highly mean here? | At a high shelf | Quietly | *Very | Happily
